  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A logic gate circuit has two inputs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and output <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>. The voltage waveforms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> are shown below</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0079_96afa86bea51.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>The logic gate circuit is</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "AND gate",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "OR gate",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "NOR gate",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "NAND gate",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Making Truth table of the given wave from,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0079_fb37d35fadcd.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 183px;\" /></p><p>It is clear from the above table that the output is present when both the inputs are high. Even when any of the input is not present, the output is low.&nbsp;This is the function of the AND gate. Hence, the logic gate present is AND gate.</p></blockquote>"
  }
